  "id": "aposematic-coloration",
  "term": "aposematic coloration",
  "definition": "Aposematic coloration is conspicuous protective body coloring in animals, such as the bright colors seen in some poison frogs. Rather than helping an animal blend in, it appears to function as part of an anti-predator strategy by honestly signaling toxicity to predators.",
